	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#ffffff"><img src="images/clear_dot.gif" alt="" width=1 height=1></td>
		<td bgcolor="#ffffff">
<p><b>by <a href="#author">Jeanette Toomer</a></b></p>
<p><font size="2">A keen observer, eloquent poet, and dynamic playwright, August Wilson thought so much of his people and culture that he set out to write a play dramatizing every decade of their lives in the 20th century.&nbsp;For his efforts he received many accolades and awards, the most prestigious of which were two Pulitzer Prizes for Drama for Fences and The Piano Lesson.&nbsp;For his works, there flowed endless gratitude and overflowing love from his people&mdash;the young and old, theatergoers, artists, producers, playwrights, directors and actors&mdash;African Americans who, through Wilson&rsquo;s plays, found new power and wealth in their heritage and cultural identity. </font></p>
<p><font size="3">On October 23rd at the new August Wilson Theater on Broadway, his people crowded the aisles and settled into seats to send upward a collective &ldquo;thank you&rdquo; to this inimitable pioneering playwright.&nbsp;Just three weeks earlier, Wilson had died from liver cancer in Seattle, Washington. At this gathering of friends, actors took the lead in attesting to the grand reach of this playwright&rsquo;s craft.&nbsp;Starletta DuPois praised his legacy saying, &ldquo;He was a self-taught man, a dreamer or dreams, a visionary chronicling a hundred years of our history</font> in a most provocative way...He made it possible to see what a brilliant, proud, humorous, creative, ingenuous, special people we are who have given mankind lessons in humanity, resourcefulness, love and healing.&rdquo;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<a name="author"></a>
<div class="greybox">
	<p><b>Jeanette Toomer</b> is a well-known journalist for <i>The Amsterdam News/></p>
</div>


